{"text": "Okay, so I need to make 24 using the numbers 1, 11, 12, and 13.", "start": 0, "end": 63, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Each number has to be used exactly once, and I can use addition, subtraction, multiplication, and division.", "start": 64, "end": 171, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Hmm, let's see.", "start": 172, "end": 187, "label": "stalling"}
{"text": "First, I should list out all the numbers: 1, 11, 12, 13.", "start": 189, "end": 245, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Since 24 is a relatively small number, maybe I can combine some of the larger numbers in a way that brings them down.", "start": 246, "end": 363, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Let me think about the bigger numbers here: 11, 12, 13.", "start": 364, "end": 419, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "If I subtract two of them, maybe?", "start": 420, "end": 453, "label": "setQuestion"}
